# r2dbsvc-control EnvironmentFile example -- CCR-14 control-plane process
# (r2db_api.control_main:app, DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md §7).
#
# Public example only. Every value below is synthetic (example.invalid / clearly
# fake secrets). Never place a real host, port, credential, or DSN in this file or
# in the copy installed at /etc/r2dbsvc/control.env; per CLAUDE.md's Public
# Repository Security Gate this repository copy is treated as public from
# creation time.
#
# This file lists every variable from r2db_api.control_main.build_control_app's
# own environment-variable contract (that module's own docstring is the
# authoritative list; DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md §7 mirrors it) explicitly --
# deliberately not relying on inheriting anything from the ambient
# shell/session environment, the same discipline deploy/env/api.env.example
# follows for the application plane. Install the real copy at
# /etc/r2dbsvc/control.env, owned root:root, mode 0600 (DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md
# §7 step 1) -- systemd reads EnvironmentFile as root before dropping to the
# service account, the same protection boundary api.env.example documents.
#
# This is a SEPARATE process from r2dbsvc-api.service (deploy/env/
# api.env.example) -- its own EnvironmentFile, its own systemd unit, its own
# listen address by default (DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md §7, R-1). Never merge this
# file with the application plane's own api.env. The two files share some
# variable *names* by design (R2DB_CREDENTIAL_PEPPER, R2DB_PLATFORM_SCHEMA,
# R2DB_PLATFORM_POOL_SIZE, R2DB_AUDIT_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS,
# R2DB_AUDIT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS) -- see each variable's own comment below for
# whether the VALUE must also match the application plane's copy, or must
# deliberately differ from it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: the r2dbsvc_controlplane role's DSN against r2dbsvc_platform
# (r2db-api/docs/POSTGRES_PROVISIONING_RUNBOOK.md §11). Never r2dbsvc_control
# -- this process must not hold provisioning authority.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_CONTROLPLANE_DSN=postgresql://r2dbsvc_controlplane:REPLACE_WITH_SECRET_MANAGER_VALUE@127.0.0.1:5432/r2dbsvc_platform

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: control-credential verifier HMAC pepper. Must DIFFER from
# R2DB_CREDENTIAL_PEPPER below -- this process refuses to start if the two
# are equal (R-2, DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK.md §7). Generate with, e.g.,
# `openssl rand -base64 32`, and store the real value only in a secret
# manager, never in this file's installed copy in plaintext outside the
# 0600 boundary.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_CONTROL_CREDENTIAL_PEPPER=REPLACE_WITH_SECRET_MANAGER_VALUE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required: the SAME application-plane credential pepper r2db_api.main uses
# (this deployment's api.env, see deploy/env/api.env.example). This process
# issues and rotates APPLICATION credentials too, via /control/v1, so its
# verifier computation must agree with the data-plane process that later
# authenticates those credentials -- control_main.py's own module docstring
# ("Deviation from the design's env-var table") explains why this is
# required here, unlike ops.py's control-credential-only CLI commands, where
# the same-named variable is optional. This VALUE must be IDENTICAL to
# api.env's own R2DB_CREDENTIAL_PEPPER -- unlike R2DB_CONTROL_CREDENTIAL_
# PEPPER above, which must differ from it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_CREDENTIAL_PEPPER=REPLACE_WITH_SECRET_MANAGER_VALUE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: control-plane resource limits (SI-08, R-7), discoverable through
# GET /control/v1/capabilities. Written out here, uncommented, at this
# codebase's current ControlPlaneLimits defaults (src/r2db_api/limits.py) --
# this file's own stated purpose is listing every variable explicitly rather
# than relying on unstated code defaults, so these are not left commented out
# even though the value shown is exactly what omitting them would already
# produce.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_CONTROL_LIMIT_APPLICATIONS=100
R2DB_CONTROL_LIMIT_CREDENTIALS_PER_APPLICATION=10
R2DB_CONTROL_LIMIT_CONTROL_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=60
# Phase 4 ledger closure L4-10: request-body byte bound, discoverable
# through GET /control/v1/capabilities' own "limits"/"limit_enforcement"
# keys and enforced by the SAME value (control_main.py's own
# ControlPlaneLimits construction -- one source for both). Default
# 1048576 (1 MiB) -- unchanged from before this variable existed
# (src/r2db_api/limits.py's own ControlPlaneLimits.request_bytes default).
R2DB_CONTROL_LIMIT_REQUEST_BYTES=1048576

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional (Phase 4, design PHASE4_DURABLE_AUDIT_SINK_V1.md D-5): audit_query's
# OWN pre-auth rate window (POST /control/v1/audit/query and its
# POST /v1/audit/query alias on this same control host) -- never shared with
# R2DB_CONTROL_LIMIT_CONTROL_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE above. Default 60. See
# r2db-api/docs/POSTGRES_PROVISIONING_RUNBOOK.md §15 for sizing guidance
# (concurrent audit consumers x 60000 / visibility_lag_ms, plus headroom for
# catch-up paging after an outage).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_CONTROL_LIMIT_AUDIT_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=60

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional (Phase 4, design D-5): the r2dbsvc_auditreader role's DSN against
# r2dbsvc_platform (migration 0007_application_audit.sql), read-only over
# BOTH control_audit and application_audit. Leave UNSET (commented out, as
# below) and audit_query (both paths above) stays declared "unavailable" --
# the routes remain registered and still authenticate the caller, answering
# CAPABILITY_UNSUPPORTED rather than a bare 404. Set it and audit_query
# becomes enabled for any caller holding a valid control/audit credential.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2DB_AUDIT_DSN=postgresql://r2dbsvc_auditreader:REPLACE_WITH_SECRET_MANAGER_VALUE@127.0.0.1:5432/r2dbsvc_platform

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional (Phase 4, design D-1/D-6): session-level timeouts set on this
# process' control_audit writer connection. Both default to 5000 (5s) if
# unset.
#
# Must be set to the SAME value as the application-plane process' own
# api.env (R2DB_AUDIT_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS / R2DB_AUDIT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS, see
# deploy/env/api.env.example) -- the two together derive the declared
# audit_query.visibility_lag_ms this process publishes through
# GET /control/v1/capabilities (statement_timeout_ms + idle_timeout_ms +
# 1000ms fixed clock-skew margin). Changing either value on either process
# changes that published declaration; see r2db-api/docs/
# POSTGRES_PROVISIONING_RUNBOOK.md §15 for the exact derivation and the
# SHOW statement_timeout / SHOW idle_in_transaction_session_timeout
# verification query.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_AUDIT_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=5000
R2DB_AUDIT_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=5000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: this process' own small dedicated pool cap -- same knob name
# r2db_api.main's own api.env sets, but scoped independently per process
# (systemd EnvironmentFile= is per-unit, so the two processes never share
# this setting). Written out explicitly at the current default (4) for the
# same reason as the limits block above.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2DB_PLATFORM_POOL_SIZE=4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional, TEST-ONLY -- do not set this in a real deployment. Identical
# escape hatch to r2db_api.main's own R2DB_PLATFORM_SCHEMA (see
# deploy/env/api.env.example's own comment on that variable for the full
# reasoning). A real control-plane deployment always uses the real
# 0005-created schema and must leave this unset.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# R2DB_PLATFORM_SCHEMA=r2dbsvc_registry
